# For-loop index name

In first-party JavaScript (not vendor files under `js/ffmpeg/`), use `ni` instead of `i` as the index in C-style `for` loops.

```javascript
// ❌ BAD
for (let i = 0; i < files.length; i++) {
    const file = files[i];
}

// ✅ GOOD
for (let ni = 0; ni < files.length; ni++) {
    const file = files[ni];
}
```

`for...of` / `for...in` loops may keep descriptive iterator names (`entry`, `tagName`, etc.). Do not rename those to `ni`.
